{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "description": "Contract-derived expected structure for the frozen lifecycle/fragment-probe-v2.1 APK. Every expected value is derived from the pinned AOSP Application.ActivityLifecycleCallbacks and android.app.FragmentManager call sites (CONTRACT.md), never from observed ATL or Android output. The scenario script (activity instance tags, call sequence) is fixed by the probe design (ProbeApp.java/ActA/ActB/FragmentProbe), which is identical on both sides. L-THROW is a TERMINAL scenario: it runs AFTER the aggregate/completion markers so the framework mCalled crash cannot destroy the reference evidence.",
  "contract": {
    "aosp_ref": "refs/tags/android-17.0.0_r1",
    "aosp_commit": "94b4c163b7dfe5ce3607f7bb8456f9573f7de57d",
    "rules": [
      "Application.mActivityLifecycleCallbacks is an ArrayList; dispatch iterates it FORWARD (registration order) for all seven callbacks (Application.java:310-320, 470-478, 578-586).",
      "Duplicate registration is additive: the same instance registered N times is invoked N times in its list positions (Application.add + dispatch).",
      "Unregister removes exactly one occurrence, the first element equal to the argument (ArrayList.remove uses argument.equals(element)) (Application.java:316-320).",
      "A dispatch uses a private toArray() snapshot (collectActivityLifecycleCallbacks, Application.java:608-616): a callback removed during dispatch still runs for the in-flight event and is absent from the next; a callback added during dispatch is absent from the in-flight event and runs from the next.",
      "Dispatch does not catch a callback exception (plain for loop): the remaining callbacks for that event are skipped and the exception propagates out of the enclosing super.*() (Application.dispatchActivity*).",
      "An observer exception thrown from onActivityCreated escapes the app's super.onCreate() (Activity.dispatchActivityCreated, Activity.java:1589-1598, runs at Activity.java:1915 BEFORE mCalled is set at Activity.java:1920). ActivityThread.performLaunchActivity sets mCalled=false before onCreate (ActivityThread.java:4550) and raises SuperNotCalledException when it is still false (ActivityThread.java:4561-4564). L-THROW is therefore a TERMINAL scenario: on Android it crashes the process, so it runs AFTER the aggregate/completion markers.",
      "The Application callback for a lifecycle method is delivered inside the app's super.<method>() call, i.e. between the probe's .pre and .post lines (Activity.java:1915,2208,2284,2721,2952,3030).",
      "Older/unknown ActivityLifecycleCallbacks default methods (onActivityPre*/Post*Created etc.) are no-ops for the probe observers, so only the seven classic callbacks are logged.",
      "On a fresh launch onActivityCreated receives a null savedInstanceState Bundle; all other basic callbacks receive no Bundle.",
      "All seven callbacks run on the ActivityThread main thread.",
      "Activity identity is the exact instance; the probe tags instances ActA#N / ActB#N.",
      "FragmentManager.findFragmentByTag scans mAdded in REVERSE add order, then mActive; duplicate tags therefore resolve to the newest-added fragment (FragmentManager.java:1847-1866).",
      "The tag is assigned at add() time but the fragment is only placed in mAdded when the transaction executes, so lookup before executePendingTransactions is null (FragmentManager.addFragment 1710-1731, BackStackRecord.executeOps).",
      "Removing an added fragment runs the destroy path (removeFragment 1734-1752, makeInactive 1697-1708, burpActive 2949-2958), which purges mActive, so a later findFragmentByTag returns null."
    ]
  },
  "identity": {
    "task_id": "ACTIVITY-LIFECYCLE",
    "probe": "lifecycle-probe-v2.1",
    "package": "org.atl.tests.lifecycle"
  },
  "acceptance_surface": {
    "surface": "lifecycle-callbacks (LC) + FragmentManager tag lookup (FT)",
    "candidate_contract": "per-(activity,event) lifecycle callback contract (mandatory event presence, and exact order/multiplicity/identity/Bundle/phase WITHIN each callback list) PLUS every FragmentManager tag scenario observation (add tag, find results, getTag, duplicate-tag newest, null/missing, pre-commit visibility, removal). Both are validated per event against the Android reference.",
    "in_scope": {
      "validated_against": "android-reference",
      "dimensions": [
        "LC per-(activity,event) callback contract",
        "FT scenario observations (add tag, find results, getTag, duplicate-tag newest, null/missing, pre-commit visibility, removal)"
      ],
      "scenario_ids": [
        "S1",
        "S2",
        "S4.1",
