        "F-REMOVE",
        "L-THROW"
      ]
    },
    "pinned": {
      "baseline_required": true,
      "dimensions": [
        "cross-Activity Activity-event ordering (the Activity-only pre/post framing sequence)"
      ],
      "note": "ONLY this single dimension is compared against the baseline. Every in_scope scenario/event is otherwise compared against the Android reference. A candidate whose Activity ordering diverges from the reference must match the baseline's Activity ordering exactly per non-terminal scenario, or it is rejected (BASELINE_MISMATCH)."
    }
  },
  "cross_activity_ordering": {
    "baseline_required": true,
    "divergence": "ATL emits the covered Activity's onStop only after the incoming Activity is resumed, and on the way back emits ActA onRestart/onStart/onResume before the outgoing Activity is stopped: that is AOSP ActivityThread ordering (handleLaunchActivity, handleStartActivity, callActivityOnStop, TransactionExecutorHelper.getLifecyclePath), but the recorded Android reference for these scenarios is event-defect-free only for the manifest groups, so the candidate carries extra ActA onStop/onRestart/onStart groups that the pin tolerates per _validate_extra_group. This is pre-existing on the ATL side and byte-identical to the ATL baseline; it is not a regression the candidate can be blamed for. See fixtures/baseline-atl.rationale.md.",
    "pin": "In PINNED mode (baseline supplied) the candidate's per-scenario Activity-only pre/post framing sequence must equal the baseline's. Scenario observations other than that single dimension (all LC callback contract values and all FT lookup values) are still validated per event against the Android reference. Candidate scenarios whose Activity ordering differs from the Android reference are reported with an explicit DIVERGENCE line instead of being rejected. A candidate Activity ordering that does not match the baseline is rejected (BASELINE_MISMATCH). Without a baseline, a candidate whose cross-Activity ordering diverges is rejected (MISSING_BASELINE, fail closed)."
  },
